From: Spaceghost <spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] include libgen for basename

Do not rely on an implicit basename declaration; modern C compilers correctly
reject treating its undeclared return value as a pointer.

---
 core.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/core.c b/core.c
--- a/core.c
+++ b/core.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <dirent.h>
 #include <errno.h>
+#include <libgen.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
-- 
